    "claim": "Building libhollis.so where cdn.pyke.io is blocked (the CCR sandbox egress proxy 403s the ort-sys prebuilt download): download the official Microsoft onnxruntime-linux-x64-1.24.2.tgz from GitHub releases, then build with ORT_LIB_LOCATION=<extracted>/lib (must point at the lib/ subdir) plus ORT_PREFER_DYNAMIC_LINK=1, and --features=serde_support as always. The resulting dylib then NEEDs libonnxruntime.so.1 at load time, so every process that loads it (server, mcp, nb-call) needs LD_LIBRARY_PATH=<extracted>/lib. On boxes that can reach the pyke CDN the default static download keeps the dylib self-contained - the env vars are sandbox-only, never committed anywhere.",
